### 3. STUDY BLOCKS — POSITIVAS / FILTROS
### ============================
# Los IDs se guardan de respuestas 201 para evitar IDs históricos (2, 5, etc.).

### ANA — Crear bloque Java inactivo (201); guardar ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/study-blocks
Cookie: JSESSIONID={{anaSessionId}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{anaCsrf}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Java",
  "active": false
}

> {%
client.global.set("anaBlockId", response.body.id);
%}

### ANA — Crear bloque Algoritmos activo (201); guardar ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/study-blocks
Cookie: JSESSIONID={{anaSessionId}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{anaCsrf}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Algoritmos",
  "active": true
}

> {%
client.global.set("anaSecondBlockId", response.body.id);
%}

### BOB — Crear bloque Python activo (201); guardar ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/study-blocks
Cookie: JSESSIONID={{bobSessionId}}
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{bobCsrf}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Python",
  "active": true
}

> {%
client.global.set("bobBlockId", response.body.id);
%}

